{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Storytelling", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Mirror of Matsuyama", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use reported speech (indirect speech) when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. <br/>This style of writing is common in storytelling. It allows the writer to share dialogue with the reader without always using quotation marks.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you tell people what someone has said you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past' since  you are reporting the information at a later time. You need to change the verb to the next past form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'m coming</span> to the party.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She said she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\u201d   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already</span> eaten.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> cook.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">I</span></span> didn't want to go.</li><li>Bill said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">he</span></span> didn't want to go.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>:<span class=\"italic\"> \u201cWhy are you trying to kill your stepmother?\u201d the angry father asks.</span><br/><span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>:<span class=\"italic\"> The angry father asks his daughter <span class=\"strong\">why she was trying</span> to kill her stepmother.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "She says that she would see her mother's face.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She adds that she would see her as she had been when she was young.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The daughter replies  that she wasn't trying to kill his new wife.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She hisses that the daughter was using evil magic!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Her mother explains that whenever she felt sad and lonely, she should look into the mirror. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">The mother <span class=\"strong\">is giving</span> a mirror to the child.</span><br/><br/>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">have told</span> this folktale many times.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in storytelling. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Then, the child cries as she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being given</span> a mirror.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Here is another folk tale that has <span class=\\\"strong\\\">been told</span> many times.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "When her daughter has been brought to her, she asks her to make sure that her father is  being taken care of. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Eventually she is standing at the temple while her father is being married once again. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "His new wife abhors the young girl. She is being consumed with jealousy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She was only looking in the mirror she has been given by her mother. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "temple ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building for religious practice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is standing at the temple while her father is being married once again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you write when you are giving information about myths and legends .", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to abhor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to dislike someone or something very much", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: His new wife abhors the young girl. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": " to consume ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to destroy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is being consumed with jealousy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "jealousy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling angry because someone else has what you want ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is being consumed with jealousy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "evil", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cruel: causing harm or injury to someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She hisses that the daughter was using evil magic!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to convey ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something known to someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We know the message has been conveyed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ashamed ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling shame or guilt", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The father and stepmother both feel ashamed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le08ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look up mirrors in folktales and fairy tales and make some notes on how they were used in these stories.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now write a short tale of your own involving a mirror.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Quote people when possible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the story to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Check the spelling and grammar together and correct any mistakes.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look up information used in folk tales and fairytales.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a tale with a mirror in it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use reported speech in my tale.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my story with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I check for spelling and grammar mistakes.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about myths and legends.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about reactions and behaviors in different 